  <h2>Economic study</h2>
  <p>
    How much does this treatment cost per tonne of soybean? Assuming a plant
    producing 20,000 tonnes a year - an average of 3 tonnes an hour -, the
    costs are as follows:
  </p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="table-data">
      <caption class="visually-hidden">
        Partial costs of extrusion-pressing treatment in euros per tonne
      </caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Partial costs (€/t)</th>
          <th scope="col">Extrusion-pressing</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Depreciation</th><td>3.60</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Financial charges</th><td>0.50</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Insurance, cash flow</th><td>1.15</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Maintenance</th><td>1.51</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Thermal energy</th><td>0</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Electrical energy</th><td>15.30</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Labour</th><td>10.50</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Total (€/t of beans crushed)</th><td>32.56</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    <small>Data: interest 2%, electricity €0.05775/kWh.</small>
  </p>
  <p>
    The cost, excluding raw material, of one tonne of soybean extruded then
    pressed comes to less than €35.
  </p>
  <p>
    The results in animals - poultry, laying hens, dairy cows - are detailed
    in the article
    <a href="/en/expert-insights/benefits-of-extruded-soybean-for-livestock">
      Benefits of extruded soybean for livestock</a>.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
